A||||9||Blacktree||Held Motorsports?||||1||
Z||000000||Blacktree||12-11-2001||03:51 AM||||I've seen a couple mentions of Held Motorsports, and it gave me the impression that they sell high-performance Fiero suspension parts. Ever since Ryane Motorsports went belly-up, I've been having trouble locating hi-perf suspension parts for mine Fiero.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Anyone got a link to Held Motorsports? Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000001||onfire||12-11-2001||05:19 AM||||Ask and you shall receive. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.heldmotorsports.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.heldmotorsports.com/</A> <P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||artherd||12-11-2001||06:58 AM||||Ryane never went belly up, Dave Held bought the buisness from him  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Had to move all the jigs and things over about two months, but Held *IS* Ryane...<P>Still the same great stuff, Dave is even taking it all a step furthur.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000003||88-DOHC||12-11-2001||05:01 PM||||Basicly Ryane was starting to get into other areas, namely custom stuff for imports. Because of this, the Fiero stuff was suffering. So Daryl sold the Fiero stuff off to Held so he could concentrate on the import stuff. Ironicly due to various reasons he has now stopped even doing custom import stuff. So I guess all he is left with is a few items for mustangs if anything at all.  Kind of sad, considering from what I little I have heard about Held, I would rather Daryl/Ryane still did the Feiro stuff.  While Ryane at times was really slow on delevery it always was top quality stuff. Something I can't say for other custom Fiero suspensions I have seen. All my stuff I got from Ryane before it was sold off to Held. As such, I havn't had any dealings with Held.||||reg||1
Z||000004||artherd||12-11-2001||09:12 PM||||I haden't heard that Daryl was having such difficulty  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  His designs and products stood alone as a way to make the Fiero a true exotic.    <P>I'm the opposite, I was just getting ready to grab a set of coilovers when  Ryane became held, so I never dealt with Daryl directly.<P>I have been dealing with Dave Held, on even customising furthur some of the Fiero parts, and he's been very helpful, and willing to play around and custom-engineer things with me.  He seems genuinely into the cars and extracting the best from them.<P>Good stuff.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 88-DOHC:<BR><B>Basicly Ryane was starting to get into other areas, namely custom stuff for imports. Because of this, the Fiero stuff was suffering. So Daryl sold the Fiero stuff off to Held so he could concentrate on the import stuff. Ironicly due to various reasons he has now stopped even doing custom import stuff. So I guess all he is left with is a few items for mustangs if anything at all.  Kind of sad, considering from what I little I have heard about Held, I would rather Daryl/Ryane still did the Feiro stuff.  While Ryane at times was really slow on delevery it always was top quality stuff. Something I can't say for other custom Fiero suspensions I have seen. All my stuff I got from Ryane before it was sold off to Held. As such, I havn't had any dealings with Held.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||rockcrawl||12-11-2001||09:42 PM||||I had purchased a few items from Ryane before the change. I was very satisfied although I always thought the prices were high. But what's a Fiero fanatic to do, there's no where else to go. More recently I have looked at some of Held's parts for an '88 but decided they were too expensive for what they were. Radius rods-$180, Lateral links-$174, Toe links-$264 for a total of $618. The Fierostore sells the same six pieces for $300!! I just recieved them today and they are of excellent quality, TIG welded, powdercoated, poly bushings installed. I'm not sure what my point is, except that maybe Held should reconsider their pricing. It seems they have carried over the same pricing that Ryane had. They are obviously selling parts for more than double what they need to be to make a profit. If Fierostore can buy them from a manufacturer and resell them for $300 and still come out ahead, I would think that Held as a manufacturer should be able to sell them for $300 or less. Maybe I'm out of line?||||reg||1
Z||000006||artherd||12-11-2001||10:50 PM||||Held's prices are reasonable, even good, compared to the aftermarket parts available for other cars.   Try buying a 13" 4-pot brake kit for any less for *ANY* automobile! I dare you!<P>Held/Ryane parts are top quality, I won't ride on less.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000007||AnimalGT||12-12-2001||02:21 AM||||I emailed Dave Held a few weeks ago about doing a 115mm hub conversion on a '85.  He was very pleasant and insightful.  I'll definitely be buying my suspension upgrade parts from Held.  Good quality, reasonable prices, and they seem to be true Fiero enthusiasts.<BR>Scott ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Blacktree||12-12-2001||02:51 AM||||Thanks for the info everyone. I now feel properly educated.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||Raydar||12-12-2001||09:22 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by AnimalGT:<BR><B>I emailed Dave Held a few weeks ago about doing a 115mm hub conversion on a '85.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I did the same, regarding an 88. Was not very encouraged by his response, though. <P>I met Dave at the Huntsville swap meet. Very knowledgable. Good guy! <BR>(As an aside, it seems I have heard that one of his relatives was a GM Powertrain engineer, and was involved in the design of the 4.9. GM supposedly looked at the 4.1 and all of its problems and said "Make it bulletproof." ) <P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||1
